Third-party material used by this demo
======================================

1. yolo_deepstream (third_party/yolo_deepstream, fetched by bootstrap.sh)
   Source:  https://github.com/NVIDIA-AI-IOT/yolo_deepstream
   Commit:  see third_party/YOLO_DEEPSTREAM_COMMIT (pinned; last upstream push 2024-09-25)
   License: Apache-2.0 for the repository (LICENSE.md). The file this demo
            builds, deepstream_yolo/nvdsinfer_custom_impl_Yolo/nvdsparsebbox_Yolo.cpp,
            carries an SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT header with NVIDIA's 2022
            copyright. A copy of that file is kept at src/nvdsparsebbox_Yolo.cpp
            (unmodified unless a scenario patch is applied) under those terms.
            The scenario patches in scenario/ are derivative works of that
            file and are offered under the same MIT terms.

2. DeepStream SDK headers (third_party/deepstream-includes, fetched by bootstrap.sh)
   Source:  /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/includes inside the
            nvcr.io/nvidia/deepstream:8.0-samples-multiarch container image
            (linux/arm64); the image id and digest are recorded in
            third_party/deepstream-includes/IMAGE_DIGEST after bootstrap.
   License: NVIDIA DeepStream SDK license (the LICENSE.txt copied beside the
            headers when the image ships one). The headers are compile-time
            inputs only; they are NOT redistributed in this repository and are
            git-ignored. Each user fetches them with bootstrap.sh under their
            own acceptance of NVIDIA's terms (NGC / DeepStream EULA).

3. TensorRT headers (third_party/tensorrt-includes, fetched by bootstrap.sh)
   Source:  Debian packages libnvinfer-headers-dev and libnvonnxparsers-dev
            (10.13.2.6-1+cuda13.0, arm64) from NVIDIA's public apt repository
            https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/repos/ubuntu2404/sbsa/,
            downloaded and extracted (never installed) in an arm64 container;
            the exact .deb names are in third_party/DEB_SOURCES. The
            DeepStream samples image ships only the TensorRT runtime libraries.
            nvdsinfer_custom_impl.h includes NvInfer.h and NvOnnxParser.h.
   License: NVIDIA TensorRT license (the package's copyright file is copied to
            third_party/tensorrt-includes/COPYRIGHT). Not redistributed here;
            git-ignored; fetched per user under their own acceptance.

4. CUDA runtime headers (third_party/cuda-includes, fetched by bootstrap.sh)
   Source:  Debian packages cuda-cudart-dev-13-0 and cuda-crt-13-0 (arm64 sbsa)
            from the same apt repository, extracted the same way
            (/usr/local/cuda-13.0/targets/sbsa-linux/include). Only
            cuda_runtime_api.h and what it includes are needed, through
            NvInfer.h.
   License: NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit EULA (copyright file copied to
            third_party/cuda-includes/COPYRIGHT). Same handling as (2) and (3).

Nothing under third_party/ is linked into a product by this demo; the only
build outputs are an aarch64 relocatable object and a shared library of
NVIDIA's own MIT-licensed parser, plus test executables, all under build/.
